      "title": "Maximum Subarray Sum with One Deletion",
      "slug": "maximum-subarray-sum-with-one-deletion",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "description": "## Description\n\nGiven an array of integers `nums`, find the maximum sum of a non-empty subarray with at most one element deleted.\n\nNote that the subarray after deletion must still be non-empty.\n\n### Parameters\n- `nums` (`int[]`): An array of integers.\n\n### Return Value\n- `int`: The maximum possible sum of a non-empty subarray after optionally deleting at most one element.\n\n### Constraints\n- 1 <= len(nums) <= 10^5\n- -10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\n\n### Examples\n\n**Example 1:**\n- Input: `nums = [1, -2, 0, 3]`\n- Output: `4`\n- Explanation: We can delete `-2` to get `[1, 0, 3]` which has a sum of `4`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n- Input: `nums = [1, -2, -2, 3]`\n- Output: `3`\n- Explanation: We can choose `[3]` or delete one `-2` from `[1, -2, 3]` to get sum `3`.",
      "functionName": "maximumSum",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "nums",
          "type": "int[]"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "int"
    },
